            "result_text": "Done! The regex has been saved to `/app/regex.txt`. \n\nHere's what it does:\n\n**IPv4 validation**: Each octet matches 0-255 without leading zeros using `(?:0|[1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])`\n\n**Date validation by month**:\n- 31-day months (Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Aug, Oct, Dec): days 01-31\n- 30-day months (Apr, Jun, Sep, Nov): days 01-30  \n- February: days 01-29\n\n**Boundaries**: Uses `(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])` and `(?![a-zA-Z0-9])` to prevent matches preceded/followed by alphanumeric characters (handles cases like \"user 1134-12-12\")\n\n**Last date only**: The negative lookahead `(?!.*\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-)` ensures no more YYYY-MM- patterns exist after the matched date, guaranteeing we capture only the last date in each line."
